  directQuestion: "Should you refactor, replatform, rebuild or replace an application?", directAnswer: "Start with the constraint: refactor when the application fits the business but its internals slow change; replatform when the runtime or hosting is the main limit; rebuild when necessary behavior cannot be evolved safely; and replace when a suitable product meets the process better. Inventory dependencies and business rules before choosing. A framework upgrade or focused integration may be enough.",
  takeaways: ["Modernization is a business-fit decision before it is a technology decision.", "Refactoring, replatforming, rebuilding and replacement solve different constraints.", "A supported framework upgrade can be more valuable than a wholesale rewrite.", "Map business rules, integrations and data before changing a critical application.", "Modernize in bounded, validated steps; preserve an exit or rollback path."],
