  faq: [
    ["What is application modernization?", "It is the targeted improvement of an existing application so that its business fit, changeability, supportability and operations remain appropriate. The intervention may be a framework upgrade, refactoring, replatforming, selective rebuild or replacement."],
    ["What is the difference between refactoring and rebuilding?", "Refactoring changes internal structure while aiming to preserve behavior. Rebuilding implements the capability again and requires rediscovering, validating and migrating behavior and data."],
    ["When should a legacy application be replaced?", "Consider replacement when the business process no longer fits and a suitable supported product can meet real requirements. Validate workflow exceptions, integration and migration obligations before deciding."],
    ["Is cloud migration the same as application modernization?", "No. Migration changes where a workload runs. Modernization changes its design, operating model or ability to serve the business. A move can include modernization, but it need not."],
    ["Can an application be modernized gradually?", "Yes. A bounded module, runtime, API or deployment path can often change first while existing capabilities continue to run. Explicit coexistence, regression testing and retirement criteria make this safer."],
    ["How do you modernize a legacy .NET application?", "Inventory framework and dependencies, business behavior and external contracts; choose the constraint to remove; test an upgrade or bounded refactoring path; and validate data, hosting and deployment before cutover. The same decision discipline applies to other stacks."],
  ], sources: [sources.aws, sources.azure, sources.dotnet, sources.azureStyles], finalEyebrow: "Modernize the constraint, not everything", finalHeadline: "What is actually preventing your application from moving forward?", finalBody: "Start with the business requirement, architecture and operating burden before choosing whether to refactor, replatform, rebuild or replace.", finalCta: "Review Your Modernization Path", related: [{ label: "12 signs your legacy application is becoming a business risk", to: "/insights/legacy-application-business-risk" }, { label: "Cloud migration vs cloud modernization", to: "/insights/cloud-migration-vs-cloud-modernization" }, { label: "Cloud-native modernization case study", to: "/case-studies/cloud-native-dotnet-modernization" }],
